      "beats": [
        {
          "zone": "offer",
          "index": 0,
          "text": "A visitor offers samples, a poster, and a gift at the BHS. Mimi asks: What is the product and expected return? She pauses acceptance.",
          "start_ms": 0,
          "end_ms": 13200
        },
        {
          "zone": "policy-topics",
          "index": 1,
          "text": "The two policies have different scopes: covered breastmilk substitutes and related products under the Milk Code; prescription products and medical devices under the pharmaceutical order.",
          "start_ms": 13500,
          "end_ms": 25060
        },
        {
          "zone": "identify",
          "index": 2,
          "text": "Mimi checks four details: product, promotion, place and audience, and inducement. Free is not authorization. Prescription samples cannot be distributed to the public.",
          "start_ms": 25360,
          "end_ms": 39080
        },
        {
          "zone": "pause",
          "index": 3,
          "text": "Mimi says: I will not accept or distribute these items. I will refer the details to the supervisor. She cannot approve an exception independently.",
          "start_ms": 39380,
          "end_ms": 49580
        },
        {
          "zone": "information",
          "index": 4,
          "text": "Mimi uses approved information without brand endorsement. Reports contain facts, without patient data. Do not blame families; refer clinical questions to a health professional.",
          "start_ms": 49880,
          "end_ms": 64360
        },
        {
          "zone": "summary",
          "index": 5,
          "text": "A promotional gift and an educational model differ. Verify the rules: recognize, pause, and refer. An educational label is insufficient; the BHW does not approve independently.",
